#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""sinter — fuse generation testimony and recipe into one firing, then assay it.

A generated file both *claims* a parent (the receipt it already carries) and
*belongs* to a firing (the generator's output list + import closure). kiln
reconstructs lots from recipes. clutch reconstructs lots from receipts.
sinter is the joint verb: one firing, witnessed two ways, then one of
RAGGED / STALE / CLEAN with a typed why (content vs clock vs dirty-parent).

Not `kiln | clutch`. Not a tag bag. The object is the assay.
"""
